* audio_fit.lib: datasheet-fit behavioural models for the AUDIO group (spice.source: fit), pass C 2026-10-23.
* Why fits: the TI vendor PSpice models (SBOM396 OPA161x, SBOM958 OPA1622) were unpacked and translated for ngspice
* (lib/spice/opa161x_ti.lib, opa1622_ti.lib: VSWITCH->SW, IF()->?:, TEMP->temper, R_NOISELESS->noisy=0), but their
* transient run did not converge in ngspice-42 (timestep too small in the ESD/OL switches, 900 s timeout): unused.
* Tags: [V] TI product page (2026-10-22), [M] recalled datasheet figure, not re-read, [E] estimate.
* Node 0 is the audio ground (AGND and GND are both ground nets in hwflow, node 0).

* min/max/clamps are smooth (0.5(a+b +- sqrt((a-b)^2+e))): kinks stalled the board transients (timestep too small)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- one op-amp section
* ports: inp inn vpos vneg out en   (en: 1 = on; tie to vpos through kon for parts without EN)
* RN: input series resistor, its thermal noise is the input voltage noise en = sqrt(4kT RN)
* AOL, GBW: single-pole open loop. VS0: output swing limit to each rail at no load. ROUT: output resistance
* outside the loop (sets the swing loss at current, ROUT x Iout, and the open-loop Zout).
* ILP / ILN: datasheet source / sink current limit [A], NOT enforced (Newton convergence): R29 measures the peak current against it. K0, FZ: supply rejection, input-referred error
* K0 x (1 + f/FZ) x (V+ - V-), i.e. PSRR = -20log(K0) dB below FZ, falling 20 dB/dec above.
* IQ: quiescent current per section, drawn from vpos to vneg (times en).  Output current is drawn from the rails.
* VCM (delta 1, D1): input common-mode window = (V-) + VCM .. (V+) - VCM (datasheet linear CM range). Node cmh =
* smooth min of the two headrooms (V; < 0 = outside the window): measure v(x<ref>.xa.cmh). ERRCM adds an input
* error ERRCM x (V outside the window), so a violation also shows as distortion [E]. VCM = 0, ERRCM = 0: no effect.
* Output stage gated by the supply span (ks: 0 below 2 V, 1 above 3 V): an unpowered section has no output current
* path into its rail nodes (stage 5: the ungated fit pumped a switched-off rail).
.subckt OPA_SEC inp inn vpos vneg out kon params: RN=73.7 AOL=3.16e6 GBW=40e6 VS0=0.6 ROUT=10 ILP=0.03 ILN=0.03
+ K0=1e-6 FZ=1e3 IQ=3.6m VCM=0 ERRCM=0
Rn inp ip {RN}
Rcm ip 0 1e12 noisy=0
Rcm2 inn 0 1e12 noisy=0
* supply-rejection path (lead network, noiseless G resistors)
Bps a1 0 V = v(vpos)-v(vneg)
G1 a1 a2 a1 a2 {K0}
C1 a1 a2 {K0/(6.2832*FZ)}
G2 a2 0 a2 0 1
* transconductance stage into the dominant pole (1 mS into AOL/1m || 1m/(2 pi GBW)), swing clamped by sharp diodes
* (exponential: Newton keeps a slope, unlike min/max) to VS0 inside each rail
Bcmh cmh 0 V = 0.5*((v(inp)-v(vneg)-{VCM})+(v(vpos)-{VCM}-v(inp))-sqrt(((v(inp)-v(vneg)-{VCM})-(v(vpos)-{VCM}-v(inp)))*((v(inp)-v(vneg)-{VCM})-(v(vpos)-{VCM}-v(inp)))+1e-4))
Bgm 0 p I = 1m*(v(ip)-v(inn)+v(a2)-{K0}*9-{ERRCM}*0.5*(sqrt(v(cmh)*v(cmh)+1e-4)-v(cmh)))
Gp p 0 p 0 {1m/AOL}
Cp p 0 {1m/(6.2832*GBW)}
* clamp diodes N = 1 (N = 0.1 stalled the board transient, timestep too small); the knee sits 0.55 V inside hi/lo
* (1e-15 x exp(0.55/0.0257) = 2 nA at the knee, 1 mA at +0.35 V), so the swing limit stays VS0 from each rail
* unpowered or collapsing rails (ADC_4V5 off, start-up): hi and lo stop at the rail midpoint instead of crossing (crossed
* clamps conduct in series, kA in the model)
Bhi hi 0 V = 0.5*((v(vpos)-{VS0}-0.55)+(0.5*(v(vpos)+v(vneg))+0.01)+sqrt(((v(vpos)-{VS0}-0.55)-(0.5*(v(vpos)+v(vneg))+0.01))*((v(vpos)-{VS0}-0.55)-(0.5*(v(vpos)+v(vneg))+0.01))+1e-4))
Blo lo 0 V = 0.5*((v(vneg)+{VS0}+0.55)+(0.5*(v(vpos)+v(vneg))-0.01)-sqrt(((v(vneg)+{VS0}+0.55)-(0.5*(v(vpos)+v(vneg))-0.01))*((v(vneg)+{VS0}+0.55)-(0.5*(v(vpos)+v(vneg))-0.01))+1e-4))
Dhi p hi DCLAMPA
Dlo lo p DCLAMPA
* XTI=0, EG small: no temperature drift of the behavioural clamp (the default law made its leakage noise dominate at 40 C)
.model DCLAMPA D(IS=1e-15 N=1 XTI=0 EG=0.01 TNOM=25)
Bks ks 0 V = 0.5*((0.5*((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)+(0)+sqrt(((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)-(0))*((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)-(0))+1e-4)))+(1)-sqrt(((0.5*((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)+(0)+sqrt(((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)-(0))*((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))*((0.5*((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)+(0)+sqrt(((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)-(0))*((v(vpos)-v(vneg)-2)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))+1e-4))
Bi ni 0 V = v(kon)*v(ks)*(v(p)-v(out))/{ROUT}
Bout 0 out I = v(ni)
* the rails supply the output current (smooth split, sqrt rounding 10 uA)
Bsrc vpos 0 I = 0.5*(v(ni)+sqrt(v(ni)*v(ni)+1e-10))
Bsnk 0 vneg I = 0.5*(sqrt(v(ni)*v(ni)+1e-10)-v(ni))
* Iq falls to 0 below 2 V of supply (an unpowered part draws nothing; a constant Iq drove the switched-off ADC_4V5 to -33 V)
Bq vpos vneg I = {IQ}*v(kon)*0.5*((0.5*(((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)+(0)+sqrt((((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)-(0))*(((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)-(0))+1e-4)))+(1)-sqrt(((0.5*(((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)+(0)+sqrt((((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)-(0))*(((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))*((0.5*(((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)+(0)+sqrt((((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)-(0))*(((v(vpos)-v(vneg))/2)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))+1e-4))
Rleak out 0 1e9 noisy=0
* supply-reversal (substrate) diode V- -> V+ of a real op-amp (delta 1): a switched-off V- rail cannot float above
* V+ + 0.6 V; without it the op found a false solution with MIC_VN at +1.6 kV (rails crossed, clamps at their midpoint)
Dsub vneg vpos DSUBA
.model DSUBA D(IS=1e-14 N=1 XTI=0 EG=0.01 TNOM=25)
.ends OPA_SEC

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- OPA1612 dual (SOIC-8)
* pins in port order: 3 (+A) 2 (-A) 1 (outA) 5 (+B) 6 (-B) 7 (outB) 8 (V+) 4 (V-)
* en 1.1 nV/rtHz [V] (RN 73.7 ohm at 300 K), GBW 40 MHz [V], AOL 130 dB [M], swing 0.6 V from the rails at 2 k [V],
* ROUT 10 ohm [E], Iout +-30 mA [V], Iq 3.6 mA/ch [V], PSRR 120 dB to 1 kHz falling 20 dB/dec [M].
* Not modelled: 1/f noise (corner ~ 100 Hz class [M], A-weighting suppresses it), current noise 1.7 pA/rtHz [M], slew 27 V/us.
* Input CM range (V-) + 2 V to (V+) - 2 V (SBOS450C p.5, delta review D1): VCM 2, ERRCM 0.1 [E].
.subckt OPA1612_DUAL_FIT inpa inna outa inpb innb outb vpos vneg
Vkon kon 0 DC 1
XA inpa inna vpos vneg outa kon OPA_SEC params: RN=73.7 GBW=40e6 VS0=0.6 ROUT=10 ILP=0.03 ILN=0.03 K0=1e-6 FZ=1e3 IQ=3.6m VCM=2 ERRCM=0.1
XB inpb innb vpos vneg outb kon OPA_SEC params: RN=73.7 GBW=40e6 VS0=0.6 ROUT=10 ILP=0.03 ILN=0.03 K0=1e-6 FZ=1e3 IQ=3.6m VCM=2 ERRCM=0.1
.ends OPA1612_DUAL_FIT

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- OPA1622 dual (VSON-10) with EN
* pins in port order: 1 (+A) 10 (-A) 9 (outA) 5 (+B) 6 (-B) 7 (outB) 2 (V+) 4 (V-) 8 (EN) 3 (GND)
* en 2.8 nV/rtHz [V] (RN 478 ohm), GBW 32 MHz [V], Iout +145 / -130 mA [V], Iq 2.6 mA/ch [V], shutdown < 5 uA [V];
* swing VS0 0.3 V + 5 ohm x Iout (0.75 V at 90 mA) [M]; PSRR 110 dB to 1 kHz falling 20 dB/dec [M];
* EN on above GND + 1.0 V (0.8-1.2 V ramp) [M].
.subckt OPA1622_DUAL_FIT inpa inna outa inpb innb outb vpos vneg en gnd
Bkon kon 0 V = 0.5*((0.5*(((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)-(0))*(((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)-(0))+1e-4)))+(1)-sqrt(((0.5*(((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)-(0))*(((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))*((0.5*(((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)-(0))*(((v(en)-v(gnd)-0.8)/0.4)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))+1e-4))
XA inpa inna vpos vneg outa kon OPA_SEC params: RN=478 GBW=32e6 VS0=0.3 ROUT=5 ILP=0.145 ILN=0.130 K0=3.16e-6 FZ=1e3 IQ=2.6m
XB inpb innb vpos vneg outb kon OPA_SEC params: RN=478 GBW=32e6 VS0=0.3 ROUT=5 ILP=0.145 ILN=0.130 K0=3.16e-6 FZ=1e3 IQ=2.6m
.ends OPA1622_DUAL_FIT

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- LT3045 positive LDO, SET-pin reference
* ports: in out gnd set en.  OUT follows V(SET) (ISET 100 uA into RSET, CSET filters); unity buffer noise
* 2 nV/rtHz (RN 241 ohm) [M: LT3045 front page "2 nV/rtHz at 10 kHz, 0.8 uVrms 10 Hz-100 kHz"];
* PSRR K0 110 dB, zero FZ 30 kHz (-> 76 dB at 1 MHz) [M: front page "76 dB at 1 MHz"]; dropout 0.26 V [M];
* limit 0.5 A [M]; IQ 2.2 mA [M]; EN/UV on above 1.24 V [M], off: no output, IQ 1 uA.
.subckt LT3045_FIT in out gnd set en params: ISET=100u RN=241 K0=3.16e-6 FZ=30k VDROP=0.26 ILIM=0.5 IQ=2.2m ROUT=0.1
* ROUT 0.1 ohm [E] (20 mohm stalled the board transient; the load steps here are mA, 0.1 mV)
* output: transconductance 1/ROUT toward o1 (linear, the input supplies it); current limit ILIM not enforced
Bkon kon gnd V = 0.5*((0.5*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))+(1)-sqrt(((0.5*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))*((0.5*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))+1e-4))
Bset in set I = {ISET}*v(kon,gnd)
Rn set sn {RN}
Rsn sn gnd 1e12 noisy=0
Bps a1 gnd V = v(in,gnd)
G1 a1 a2 a1 a2 {K0}
C1 a1 a2 {K0/(6.2832*FZ)}
G2 a2 gnd a2 gnd 1
Bo o1 gnd V = 0.5*((0.5*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)+(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP})-sqrt(((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP}))*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP}))+1e-6)))+(0)+sqrt(((0.5*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)+(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP})-sqrt(((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP}))*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP}))+1e-6)))-(0))*((0.5*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)+(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP})-sqrt(((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP}))*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)-{VDROP}))+1e-6)))-(0))+1e-6))
Bx x gnd V = v(kon,gnd)*(v(o1,gnd)-v(out,gnd))/{ROUT}
Bout gnd out I = v(x,gnd)
Bdraw in gnd I = v(x,gnd)
Bq in gnd I = {IQ}*v(kon,gnd) + 1u
Rmin out gnd 100k noisy=0
.ends LT3045_FIT

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- LT3094 negative LDO, SET-pin reference
* ports: in out gnd set en (in, out negative). SET current 100 uA out of the SET node toward IN, so
* V(SET) = -ISET x RSET; same noise/PSRR class as LT3045 [M: front page "0.8 uVrms, 74 dB at 1 MHz"]; dropout 0.235 V [M];
* limit 0.5 A [M]; IQ 2.3 mA [M]. EN/UV tied to IN in this design: enabled when |V(en)| > 1.24 V.
.subckt LT3094_FIT in out gnd set en params: ISET=100u RN=241 K0=3.16e-6 FZ=30k VDROP=0.235 ILIM=0.5 IQ=2.3m ROUT=0.1
Bkon kon gnd V = 0.5*((0.5*(((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))+(1)-sqrt(((0.5*(((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))*((0.5*(((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((-v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))+1e-4))
Bset set in I = {ISET}*v(kon,gnd)
Rn set sn {RN}
Rsn sn gnd 1e12 noisy=0
Bps a1 gnd V = v(in,gnd)
G1 a1 a2 a1 a2 {K0}
C1 a1 a2 {K0/(6.2832*FZ)}
G2 a2 gnd a2 gnd 1
Bo o1 gnd V = 0.5*((0.5*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)+(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP})+sqrt(((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP}))*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP}))+1e-6)))+(0)-sqrt(((0.5*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)+(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP})+sqrt(((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP}))*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP}))+1e-6)))-(0))*((0.5*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)+(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP})+sqrt(((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP}))*((v(sn,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)+{K0}*5)-(v(in,gnd)+{VDROP}))+1e-6)))-(0))+1e-6))
Bx x gnd V = v(kon,gnd)*(v(o1,gnd)-v(out,gnd))/{ROUT}
Bout gnd out I = v(x,gnd)
Bdraw gnd in I = -v(x,gnd)
Bq gnd in I = {IQ}*v(kon,gnd) + 1u
Rmin out gnd 100k noisy=0
.ends LT3094_FIT

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- ADP7118 adjustable LDO
* ports: in out gnd adj en.  Loop holds V(ADJ) = 1.2 V [M]; output noise ~11 uVrms 10 Hz-100 kHz (35 nV/rtHz at the
* 4.5 V output, put at the reference: 9.3 nV/rtHz -> RN 5.3 k) [M]; PSRR 95 dB with a zero at 5 kHz (88 dB at 10 kHz,
* 69 dB at 100 kHz) [M], applied at the reference scaled by 1.2/4.5; dropout 0.2 V; limit 0.36 A [M] (rating 200 mA);
* IQ 0.4 mA [M]; EN on above 1.2 V. Error amplifier: transconductance GM 100 A/V (no integrator: DC convergence).
.subckt ADP7118_FIT in out gnd adj en params: VREF=1.2 RN=5.3k K0=4.7e-6 FZ=5k VDROP=0.2 ILIM=0.36 IQ=0.4m GM=20
* error transconductance GM (A/V) into the output node: loop crossover GM x beta / (2 pi Cout) ~ 85 kHz with 10 uF (GM 100 stalled the board transient)
Bkon kon gnd V = 0.5*((0.5*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))+(1)-sqrt(((0.5*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))*((0.5*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)+(0)+sqrt((((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))*(((v(en,gnd)-1.1)/0.3)-(0))+1e-4)))-(1))+1e-4))
Vr r0 gnd DC {VREF}
Rn r0 r1 {RN}
Rr1 r1 gnd 1e12 noisy=0
Bps a1 gnd V = v(in,gnd)
G1 a1 a2 a1 a2 {K0}
C1 a1 a2 {K0/(6.2832*FZ)}
G2 a2 gnd a2 gnd 1
* dropout and current limit not enforced (Newton convergence); R29 checks the rail and the 200 mA rating
Bpass in out I = v(kon,gnd)*{GM}*(v(r1,gnd)+v(a2,gnd)-{K0}*5.5-v(adj,gnd))
Bq in gnd I = {IQ}*v(kon,gnd) + 1u
Rmin out gnd 100k noisy=0
.ends ADP7118_FIT

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- supply pre-filter ferrite with coupled-noise injection
* ports: a b. BLM18PG121SN1D: DCR 0.05 ohm, ~1 uH at audio frequencies [M]. In series: E sources from the global
* testbench nodes vbn (host VBUS / converter noise on the supply, R22) and gdn (shared-ground drop, R22). Both are
* 0 V unless the testbench turns them on, so the bead is an ordinary L + R otherwise.
* Rp 120 ohm across L1: the bead's resistive impedance (120 ohm at 100 MHz, the part's rating [M]); without it the
* 1 uH + 10 uF LDO input cap is a Q ~ 30 resonator that stalled the bus_3a start-up (timestep too small at xfb952.x1).
* Rp leaves the audio band unchanged (|j w L| = 0.13 ohm at 20 kHz << 120 ohm).
.subckt FB_INJ a b
E1 a x1 vbn 0 1
E2 x1 x2 gdn 0 1
L1 x2 x3 1u
Rp1 x2 x3 120
R1 x3 b 0.05
.ends FB_INJ

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- TPD1E10B06 ESD diode at an audio contact
* ports: io gnd. 12 pF, leakage <= 100 nA at 5.5 V (55 Mohm) [M]; clamping not modelled (signals stay within +-5 V).
.subckt TVS_FIT io gnd
C1 io gnd 12p
R1 io gnd 55meg
.ends TVS_FIT
